                        "form": "vicariantes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "98c04ce2-ce0a-3355-9f69-f3721f584b09",
                        "entry_id": "2463d24f-62c7-3da6-b4cd-a1e10c427a00",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui remplace quelque chose d’autre."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "literary"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f7a7d5ae-8c79-3db6-8405-b8d75f0a24fb",
                        "entry_id": "2463d24f-62c7-3da6-b4cd-a1e10c427a00",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qualifie une espèce, animale ou végétale, qui remplace une espèce voisine dans la même niche écologique."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "especially"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f2b03253-dc6f-49c9-bf20-a7035ed77500",
                                "sense_id": "f7a7d5ae-8c79-3db6-8405-b8d75f0a24fb",
                                "text": "Certaines espèces de Culicoïdes ont été incriminées comme vecteurs vicariants d'Oncocerca cœcutiens (p. 196) et d'Acanthocheilonema perstans (p. 194)."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4c63513b-aa63-3296-a929-e4c3de73f079",
                        "entry_id": "2463d24f-62c7-3da6-b4cd-a1e10c427a00",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Appris indirectement, en marge du discours du maître proprement dit."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "119bac95-65c7-4553-8de0-0c46170d2b1a",
                                "sense_id": "4c63513b-aa63-3296-a929-e4c3de73f079",
                                "text": "L’enfant peut, en regardant le professeur écrire, marcher, ou s’adresser aux autres enfants, apprendre beaucoup de choses de manière consciente ou inconsciente. C’est le propre de l’apprentissage vicariant, qu’on appelle aussi : Apprentissage Social."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0eec8065-11cb-361e-9725-c04af2b63e3f",
                        "entry_id": "2463d24f-62c7-3da6-b4cd-a1e10c427a00",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Éprouvant des émotions d’autres personnes par proximité avec celles-ci."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "841024d9-207a-43af-9139-a2f0009c3d8c",
                                "sense_id": "0eec8065-11cb-361e-9725-c04af2b63e3f",
                                "text": "Eh bien… je pense qu’inconsciemment vous avez masqué le traumatisme de la mort de votre père et celui d’avoir été abandonnée par votre mère par des traumatismes vicariants dus à votre travail. On souffre de la douleur des autres pour camoufler la sienne."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ea89376e-4436-4275-8afd-a43cb136f2d2",
                                "sense_id": "0eec8065-11cb-361e-9725-c04af2b63e3f",
                                "text": "La fatigue par compassion, souvent appelée le traumatisme vicariant, est une absorption de la détresse de l’autre où l’intervenant ressent lui-même cette fatigue. Celle-ci est bien connue chez les intervenants de première ligne (policiers, infirmières, pompiers, psychologues et thérapeutes, et même chez les vétérinaires)."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "442f7262-b6c5-42c0-a2b3-34a4f2c1778b",
                        "source_entry_id": "2463d24f-62c7-3da6-b4cd-a1e10c427a00",
                        "target_lang_word": "vicarious",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "vicarious",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9b02e458-5393-316e-81f0-a36e463b3146",
                                        "entry_id": "0c5ff814-ebdc-3d81-8779-9f52555a0c6e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Delegated."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3dbebd1b-b67b-3554-a6ab-2def2cc089af",
                                        "entry_id": "0c5ff814-ebdc-3d81-8779-9f52555a0c6e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Experienced or gained by taking in another person’s experience rather than through first-hand experience, such as through watching or reading."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a07d20aa-c9ce-4cdf-be7b-0c3da5fdc143",
                                                "sense_id": "3dbebd1b-b67b-3554-a6ab-2def2cc089af",
                                                "text": "People experience vicarious pleasures through watching television."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b8789145-39a9-4793-b969-4e7506dccbd2",
                                                "sense_id": "3dbebd1b-b67b-3554-a6ab-2def2cc089af",
                                                "text": "The pleasures which I made haste to seek in my disguise were, as I have said, undignified; I would scarce use a harder term. But in the hands of Edward Hyde, they soon began to turn toward the monstrous. When I would come back from these excursions, I was often plunged into a kind of wonder at my vicarious depravity."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "70c2912d-ec81-42dd-96d7-668005a45d06",
                                                "sense_id": "3dbebd1b-b67b-3554-a6ab-2def2cc089af",
                                                "text": "These are people getting some sort of vicarious thrill from the street violence people like Tommy Robinson promote. Those that are attacking Jess Philips, who I'm proud to call colleague and a friend, are not protecting victims."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "59ae4768-73f7-3c83-8e7e-d1ecaa8b4273",
                                        "entry_id": "0c5ff814-ebdc-3d81-8779-9f52555a0c6e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "On behalf of others."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "34d936e0-1da4-4849-9729-37a7acb3ec8e",
                                                "sense_id": "59ae4768-73f7-3c83-8e7e-d1ecaa8b4273",
                                                "text": "The concept of vicarious atonement, that one person can atone for the sins of another, is found in many religions."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "12559516-5074-4833-96e7-4ccefd47b431",
                                                "sense_id": "59ae4768-73f7-3c83-8e7e-d1ecaa8b4273",
                                                "text": "As time went on, the cruel custom was so far mitigated that a ram was accepted as a vicarious sacrifice in room of the royal victim."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0e546484-64fc-43d3-b3c3-f78733545413",
                                                "sense_id": "59ae4768-73f7-3c83-8e7e-d1ecaa8b4273",
                                                "text": "In these, however, he had not much time to indulge, for a footman, still decked in the trappings of vicarious grief, opened the door with the most startling promptitude, and he was ushered upstairs into a small but richly furnished room."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
